{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PHASE 2 COMPLETE — epic 6202 claimed (open -> in_progress).\n\nPlan-review needed TWO runs. The first returned INDETERMINATE with zero blocking findings and exit 2, cause `llm-degrade: NEEDS_INVESTIGATION — Unclassified failure` — LLM infrastructure, not a plan defect (prior tickets exist for the same condition on completion-verify). Retried: PASS, signed at head_sha ebbcd7a030d6029216127c83fb43c415117af366.\n\n## Eight advisories to carry into the leaf work — four are substantive\n\n- **G4 (real cross-ticket conflict):** S4's /var/tmp SIZE CAP conflicts with sibling 3e92 (scowlful-bovine-dragonfly), which documents `/var/tmp/rebar-evidence/<ticket>-<stamp>/` as the trap-cleaned evidence location. Capping /var/tmp without accounting for that location would either evict evidence mid-investigation or make the documented location unusable. S4 must reconcile the two — this is the kind of thing that only shows up when two tickets are read together.\n- **G4 (scope overlap):** S2 and S5 share implicit state over Docker overlay2 accounting and prune behaviour. S2 caps overlay2/BuildKit; S5 bounds writable container layers — which live IN overlay2. Their caps interact and must be designed as one budget, not two independent ones.\n- **G3 (coverage gap):** parent AC4 ('existing root/data disk alarms remain present; the cyclopean missing-data fix is not regressed') is NOT covered by the union of the children's ACs. No child asserts the non-regression. Needs an explicit check in whichever leaf lands last, or its own criterion.\n- **T2 (the unspecified numbers):** the whole architecture rests on cap VALUES (Docker maxUsedSpace/--keep-storage, journald SystemMaxUse, /var/tmp quota, gate-scratch EBS size) and per-generator alarm thresholds that the plan does not fix. Same shape as the 9ea3 memory-limit problem: a number chosen without measurement is a guess. The measured breakdown from bug 3276 is the grounding available — root 28G of which /var/lib/docker 17G (overlay2 16G), /var/tmp 3.6G, /var/log 1.8G (journal 1.7G).\n- P5 confirms independently what preflight found: S2-S5 touch the same files with no ordering edge.\n- ISF: the plan does not reference this session log; cosmetic.\n\n## Second gate memory measurement (feeds bug 9ea3 AC5)\n\nRun 1 (degraded early): peak 752 MB / delta 501 MB / 118s. Run 2 (complete): peak 1000 MB / **delta 739 MB** / 281s. So a COMPLETE plan-review on a 6-child container ticket costs ~739 MB resident growth over ~4.7 min, and cost varies materially between runs. Recorded on 9ea3.\n\nNEXT: claim S0 (7dfa livid-blondish-shearwater, the ADR) — the only ready leaf."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788477686608747001,"uuid":"49e7b9b0-07e4-4fee-98e0-d370fafc5162"}